## Goal
Perform unsupervised Principal Component Analysis (PCA) on the gene count matrix to visualize 
sample relationships in reduced space, colored by treatment condition (treated vs untreated).

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_samplesheets | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk.design.csv |

## Method
1. Load the gene count matrix from the counts_gene artifact and the design table using Python 
   (pandas, scikit-learn) in the gars-bio environment.
2. Apply log2 transformation with pseudocount (log2(counts + 1)) to normalize the distribution.
3. Fit PCA with two principal components to the log-transformed counts using scikit-learn's 
   PCA() with `n_components=2`. Center and scale the data automatically (default).
4. Extract PC1 and PC2 scores for each sample.
5. Merge PCA scores with sample metadata from the design table to retrieve the treatment 
   condition for each sample.
6. Generate a scatter plot showing PC1 vs PC2, coloring points by condition (treated vs 
   untreated), using matplotlib.
7. Save PCA coordinates (sample_id, PC1, PC2, condition) as a table in results/.
8. Save the plot as results/pca_plot.png.
9. Run locally as a small analysis that completes in < 1 minute on 6 samples.

